  "coverage": [
    "Exact sole-consumer source dataflow identifies a normal scalar Matrix comprehension followed only by identity aliases and MatrixTranspose. All seven native scalar kinds are supported. The original row builder can finalize directly in the selected column shape, preserving every bit and empty geometry. Escaped intermediates, block/rectangular results and incompatible grouping retain the existing route.",
    "The same Cranelift numeric-map DAG, word producer or ordinary checked collection producer fills its original typed bank. No second arithmetic engine, per-element dispatch or source rewrite is introduced. The original row Value and transpose copy are elided only after complete selected-factory, source/output shape, logical constructor and finite coexistence checks.",
    "Complete original constructor and transpose bounds cover bytes/elements, cloned/comparison/compute work, temporary storage, nodes, old owners, physical claims and full ordinary finish/call replay credit. An inadmissible optional attempt retains ordinary execution. A failed producer still reports its original arithmetic/index error. Existing direct scalar native execution and exact Core typed constructors remain maintained.",
    "The original collection finish has a separately funded checked helper. A tracked canonical column Value remains private across exact original continuation visits. It publishes into the original transpose output slot AFTER its original admission and retirement, preserving repeated-loop generations, immutable aliases, atomic outputs and cleanup. Managed native transport remains zero; the shared post-action join preserves all later source behavior.",
    "Six focused original/decoded/Object/restored tests cover all seven kinds including exact F64 NaN/zero/infinity bits, empty and two-dimensional source shapes, independent word/native producers, nine finite dimensions and distinct old outputs, nested repeated builders, real activation checkpoints, inactive and partial bad reads, mutations/interleaving, exact table-image forgery, ordinary escaped/shape routes and retry. Actual Deriche/Gram-Schmidt/Durbin checks require direct transpose publication. The protocol tag round-trip test is also run explicitly."
  ],
